    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green \u2014 **38 tests, 0 failures**, including the two new `Cp27Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a derived, read-only value on the owner GET response. The response DTO is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated via a MapStruct mapper, so I wired it into both layers, matching the existing pattern used for `membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` backed by a helper:\n   ```java\n   default String contactPreference(Owner owner) {\n       boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty();\n       return hasEmail ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThis returns `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise, using the same email-presence check the existing `membershipLevel` logic already relies on.",
